 "intro_html": "Korea's best-known beef dish: thin slices of tender beef marinated in <b>soy, grated pear, garlic and sesame</b>, then seared quickly so the edges caramelise. Pre-sliced bulgogi beef is hard to find, so this recipe shows how to slice it yourself: <b>half-freeze a piece of sirloin or ribeye</b> and it cuts thin and even with an ordinary sharp knife. A <b>steel pan</b> is perfect here: get it very hot and cook in small batches so the meat sears instead of stewing. Leftovers go into <a href=\"bibimbap.html\">bibimbap</a>. For a version with no slicing, see <a href=\"dak-bulgogi.html\">chicken bulgogi</a>. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
